You are building inside the Hypergro deploy boilerplate. Follow the project rules.

- Canonical rules: @.ai/master-prompt.md
- Architecture + add-a-resource recipe: @.ai/architecture.md
- Stack, single-port model, statelessness, naming: @.ai/standards.md
- Data & files (MongoDB + GCS, never local disk): @.ai/data-storage.md
- What you must never edit + how deploys work: @.ai/deploy.md

Non-negotiables: Express+TypeScript backend and Next.js+TypeScript frontend,
MongoDB only; never write to local disk (data → MongoDB, files → GCS via
backend/src/Repository/external/gcs.ts); never edit the Dockerfile, server.js, or
frontend/next.config.mjs proxy; never hardcode secrets (read env only via
backend/src/Config/AppConfig.ts); add API endpoints as explicit Express routes
under /api/* following Route→Validator→Controller→Service→Repository→Model, wired
through the DI container (backend/src/DI/) — never create Next.js API routes
for data. Keep the fixed backend layer folders: never add a new top-level folder
under backend/src/ (new features nest inside existing layers; third-party
integrations go under Repository/external/).
